**Reasoning**: The exhaustive best-improvement search over moves+swaps is already strong but gets stuck at local optima where the max KVPR cannot be lowered by any single operation. Plateau moves (which redistribute load among non-worst GPUs without changing the max) are a well-known escape mechanism and are cheap here since candidate evaluations are already computed. The plateau budget of 6 prevents infinite cycling, and any placement found is still validated by `score` before being compared, so quality can only improve. Doubling restarts uses spare time budget (0.05s → still well under limits) for more basin diversity.
